From 397bc30db0fb19a33d5075e70c2cabda14e4dd3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chiro <chiro@local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 01:01:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 155/235] feat(tools): add c8-l4-sve256 SVE256 driver backend,
 L4 judge and blocker probe

- qwen35_weighted_execution_driver: --backend sve256 (native/qemu), per-op
  execution-mode census (native vector/scalar-lane/scalar-convert/host loop/
  host_reference) and --skip-gold-alignment so the execution machine only
  needs golden input_ids (gold arrays stay on the judging machine).
- tools/c8_l4_compare.py: C8 L4 verdict (strict argmax + near-tie exception,
  max_abs <= 2x band, cosine >= band_cosine - 1e-4); band/thresholds are
  read from band.json and the path/sha256/pointer are printed.
- tools/c8_sve256_w8a8_gap_probe.py: reproduces the whole-net W8A8 lowering
  blocker (int8 weight transpose has no SVE256 layout path) and emits the
  static execution-mode census; bf16 whole-net lowers as a control.
- tools/c8_sve256_a3/: bundle/sync/fetch/diagnostic scripts for the A3
  host-side (cpus 320-639) bf16 link diagnostic.
